Page 1 of 4

Fe-Line-Mignon lights each candle for the moonlit café, then notices a new kitten sitting
alone beside the window.
Page 2 of 4

Meow-inara carries a tray of warm croissants, but every table is full. The kitten whispers
that she can simply go home.
Page 3 of 4

The guests slide their little tables together into one long moon-shaped curve. A space
appears exactly where the kitten can see everyone.
Page 4 of 4

At goodnight, the kitten asks if she may return tomorrow. Fe-Line-Mignon gives her the
candle by the window and says, “This light will save your place.”
Questions for Fe-Line-Mignon’s Moonlit Café

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: Who does Fe-Line-Mignon notice by the window?
Page 2
Talk together: Why does the kitten think she must leave?
Page 3
Talk together: How do the guests make room?
Page 4
Talk together: What promise does the candle represent?
After reading
How did the guests welcome the new kitten?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: They joined their tables and made her a place.

