Page 1 of 4

Ham-and-Cheese enters the cardboard maze certain his nose will lead him straight to the
prize. He wants to beat his fastest time.
Page 2 of 4

Inside a narrow tunnel, he hears a squeak behind a loose flap. A younger mouse has lost
both the exit and her courage.
Page 3 of 4

The cheesy smell drifts around the next turn, but Ham walks away from it to guide the
mouse outside. His old record slips away.
Page 4 of 4

They solve the route together and reach the centre from a new direction. The cheese
tastes better shared—and the mouse asks for another race.
Questions for Ham-and-Cheese’s Big Maze

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: What does Ham-and-Cheese want to achieve?
Page 2
Talk together: Who needs help inside the tunnel?
Page 3
Talk together: What does Ham give up to help the mouse?
Page 4
Talk together: Why does the prize feel better at the end?
After reading
Why did Ham-and-Cheese miss his fastest time?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: He stopped to help a lost mouse.

