Page 1 of 4

Wise Owl opens the library and finds Quill-Berry waiting outside with a folded page. “I
wrote something,” Quill whispers, “but I am not sure I can share it.”
Page 2 of 4

A gust slips through the door and carries the poem beneath a table. Quill-Berry freezes,
certain everyone will laugh if they read it.
Page 3 of 4

Meow-inara finds the page but does not read it. She returns it in the quiet corner and
asks, “Would you like one friendly listener?”
Page 4 of 4

Quill-Berry reads her story to two friends, then four, then the whole afternoon circle. Wise
Owl adds a blank page to the display for whatever Quill writes next.
Questions for Wise Owl’s Library Day

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: Why is Quill-Berry waiting at the library?
Page 2
Talk together: How does Quill-Berry feel when the poem blows away?
Page 3
Talk together: How does Meow-inara respect Quill-Berry?
Page 4
Talk together: What changed between the first and final page?
After reading
Why did returning the poem unread help Quill-Berry?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: It let Quill choose when and with whom to share. Meow-inara respected Quill and offered one
friendly listener.

