Page 1 of 4

Centi-Peed laces his many racing boots and announces he will win by one hundred steps.
Shelly-Pop quietly wishes everyone luck.
Page 2 of 4

Wise Owl claps the starting signal. Centi-Peed springs ahead so quickly that his
bootlaces hum.
Page 3 of 4

He zooms past the roses, then hears Shelly call: a fallen twig has pinned her race
number. Centi skids to a stop.
Page 4 of 4

After he frees Shelly, they cross the finish together behind the others. Centi wins no
ribbon, but all his boots join Shelly’s happiest dance.
Questions for Centi-Peed’s Garden Race

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: How is Centi-Peed feeling before the race?
Page 2
Talk together: What begins the race?
Page 3
Talk together: Why does Centi-Peed stop while leading?
Page 4
Talk together: What matters more than the ribbon at the finish?
After reading
Why did Centi-Peed stop during the race?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: To free Shelly-Pop’s trapped race number.

